    "description": "A device firmware package defines a RadioEndpoint class whose constructor is intended for the production device factory, not for application code that may instantiate endpoints by accident. The factory lives in a separate support library and must construct RadioEndpoint with a validated channel descriptor and security context. The constructor also has to remain callable through a generic make_unique-based allocation helper, so simply moving it to a private section would make the factory workflow impossible. Introduce a private capability that the factory alone can create, require that capability as the constructor's additional argument, and keep the capability type inaccessible to application code. The factory can then use the existing allocation path while direct construction is rejected during compilation. The public API must not advertise the capability or allow untrusted callers to acquire it.",
    "decision_statement": "Decide how to restrict construction of RadioEndpoint to the device factory while preserving generic allocation and compile-time rejection for all other callers.",
    "notes": "A factory-only capability token gates construction while preserving generic allocation; attorney-client is the near miss for forwarding construction through a named gateway instead."
  },
